# The home grid's user order (study 046 P1): a stored order (config home_order, the FNV-1a keys of the tiles' ids as
# comma separated hex: 2048, Calculator, Mesh, Settings, Store, Python (hidden: no tile), CLI, SSH) puts the tiles in
# that order; Browser, not in the list (a new app), comes last. Checked with expect_same against the same tiles listed
# in that order with no stored order. Then Settings > Launcher's last row "Reset app order", its question, Reset: the
# stored order is cleared and the grid is today's again (the harness reloads its tiles with `apps`; on the board the
# registry callback reloads the grid).
# Review only: no golden. The ids are the board's (harness_launch.cpp tile_id: a built-in's config key, else the
# desktop loader's id of "<name>.desktop").
title home order
review
sizes 640x480 480x800 720x720
env APPLAUNCH_DEV 0
clock 20:30
wifi 70
bt on
# today's grid with the tiles listed in the expected order, nothing stored
apps 2048=fixture:2048_128.png Calculator Mesh Settings CLI SSH Browser
home
shot home_order_expected
# the same tiles in today's order, with the stored order
config home_order 5db35fa9,1af49623,81ac1fe3,9b6f26cf,30c82f22,6cbae6b3,cd07a96d,3df2309d
apps Settings CLI SSH Calculator 2048=fixture:2048_128.png Mesh Browser
home
shot home_order_seeded
expect_same home_order_expected
# Settings > Launcher: the reset row is the section's last
launch Settings
key DOWN
key DOWN
key DOWN
key ENTER
wait 300
key UP
wait 300
shot home_order_reset_row
key ENTER
wait 300
shot home_order_reset_ask
key ENTER
wait 300
shot home_order_reset_done
# the grid reloaded: today's order
apps Settings CLI SSH Calculator 2048=fixture:2048_128.png Mesh Browser
home
shot home_order_after_reset
